{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":119841,"duration_api_ms":209769,"num_turns":6,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6407530e-ca96-4ab0-b68e-abc577872f68","total_cost_usd":0.5997434499999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":3578,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29093,"cache_read_input_tokens":79869,"output_tokens":2716,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29093,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1879,"outputTokens":11411,"cacheReadInputTokens":1216737,"cacheCreationInputTokens":89264,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.29218770000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":3578,"outputTokens":2716,"cacheReadInputTokens":79869,"cacheCreationInputTokens":29093,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.30755575,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All six amendments identify genuine correctness, robustness, or maintainability defects. The NaN silent-pass in Envelope::check and the runtime egg fabrication in enforce_invariants are the most critical (they can silently corrupt simulation outcomes). The artifact-path collision is a concrete bug that will cause debugging confusion. The NO3 bound brittleness and reproduction test issues are real but lower severity — they affect test resilience and clarity rather than simulation correctness.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-32fa1988","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed: warm_room week 8 NO3 bounds span only 1.0 mg N/L (4.5–5.5), and several others are 1.5 mg N/L, all tightly clustered around the source water's 5.0 mg N/L from moderate.toml. These bounds test source-water stability, not meaningful nitrogen-cycle behavior. With downstream beads normalizing nitrogen kinetics, these will break on any parameter tune. Widening to ±2–3 mg/L with source-water documentation is the right fix — it still catches real regressions while accommodating legitimate model evolution."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-423a179e","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: Envelope::check uses bare `snap.ph < min || snap.ph > max` comparisons on all 12 f64 fields. Under IEEE 754, NaN comparisons return false for both < and >, so a NaN value passes every bound silently. The existing final_finite assertions only fire at end-of-run, meaning the root cause of NaN propagation is obscured. Adding a per-field is_finite() guard at the top of check is a straightforward correctness fix that surfaces corruption at the earliest checkpoint rather than hours later."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-3081f78c","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: the test zeroes both mortality parameters, forces periphyton ≥5g, adult reserve ≥3g, reproductive readiness ≥0.5, and extends maturation to 120 days — six separate state manipulations before the run starts. This proves reproduction is mechanically possible under ideal conditions but provides no coverage of the natural survival pathway. Adding a doc comment labeling it as a controlled-ideal test is low-cost and prevents future misinterpretation. A companion test with only mortality zeroed (no reserve/readiness rigging) would meaningfully improve coverage."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-fe5ff040","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: reconcile_egg_cohort_counts (biology.rs:607-626) fabricates new EggCohort objects when cohort_total < berried_females_count, setting progress_days to the max of existing cohorts' progress. enforce_invariants calls this on every simulation step (engine.rs lines 790 and 794, before and after step_hours). This means a transient bookkeeping discrepancy — which should be surfaced as a bug — instead silently creates near-hatching clutches that participate in normal egg development, potentially duplicating births. This repair logic is appropriate at load/migration boundaries but dangerous as a per-step runtime operation. The validation test (lines 263-300) explicitly blesses this fabrication behavior, which normalizes a defect."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-7371c682","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: artifact_dir() returns `/tmp/tank_harness/{scenario_id}_seed{seed}`. Three tests use medium_planted with seed 42: the baseline envelope test (line 246), the DO-dips test (line 778), and the reproduction variant (line 849 via from_state, which still labels it 'medium_planted'). All three would write to `/tmp/tank_harness/medium_planted_seed42/`, overwriting each other's trace.jsonl, ledger, and metadata in a failing or parallel run. The from_state variant's artifacts are also ambiguous since they carry the same scenario_id as unmodified runs. Adding a per-run test label to the artifact path and metadata is a straightforward fix for a real debugging obstacle."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-2d8bb6d0","decision":"accept","rationale":"This overlaps with fr-1-3081f78c but makes the stronger architectural argument: if the project needs a reproduction regression test, it should be a named scenario or fixture with public startup parameters and normal mortality semantics, not a hidden-state-boosted variant that bypasses the survival/stress model entirely. As implemented, this test can continue passing after regressions in mortality, stress, or reserve accumulation because those systems are disabled or pre-seeded. Both amendments are valid — 3081f78c addresses the documentation gap, and this one addresses the design gap."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"95bdf836-f68e-4400-b26a-8056f0281278"}
